Apply ComfyUI scaled-FP8 weight scales when reading safetensors

Bare fp8 tensors were already decoded through the LUT, but the per-tensor
F32 weight_scale and scale_weight entries were ignored. A scaled-FP8 file
imported with every weight about 1/scale too large and rendered a solid
colour or NaN.

applyingScaledFP8WeightScales returns the archive unchanged when the file
carries no scales. Otherwise it returns a wrapper that multiplies each
F8_E4M3 tensor by its scale at read time. The wrapper is applied through
with(_:block:) so a gather over several sources applies each source's own
scale, which the per-element ModelWeightElement.scale cannot do.
ModelImporter wraps every SafeTensors open before architecture detection, so
the scales apply whatever the file holds. An orphan scale, a scaled E5M2
tensor, a scale for a non-FP8 tensor and an undecodable dtype each print a
warning to stderr, and the import continues.
